'''Mirmulnir''' is likely the second [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragon]] you will encounter in Skyrim, after [[Skyrim:Alduin|Alduin]]. The dragon appears during the quest [[Skyrim:Dragon Rising|Dragon Rising]] at the [[Skyrim:Western Watchtower|Western Watchtower]]. He can be a challenging enemy if your level is low and you have only melee weapons. If you are heavily injured you can go inside the watchtower to heal yourself while resting, or stay there and do nothing while the guards attack him. Using lightning or ice magic on him would be wise since he is resistant only to fire. As with other dragons, after Mirmulnir is killed you can take from his corpse [[Skyrim:Dragon Scales|dragon scales]] and [[Skyrim:Dragon Bone|dragon bones]], as well as random treasure and several [[#Notes|unique]] pieces of Whiterun guard armor.

Mirmulnir's name can be broken down into Mir Mul Nir, literally 'Allegiance Strong Hunt'.

The type of dragon that Mirmulnir is depends on your level.
