==Notes==
* The ''[[Skyrim:Atlas of Dragons|Atlas of Dragons]]'' lists Mirmulnir as being "Known to Live", meaning not likely revived by Alduin. Instead, he may have come out of hiding to again serve Alduin.
* Mirmulnir carries a random number of Whiterun guard outfit parts, which have a [[Skyrim:Permanent Items|special property]]: if sold to a merchant, they will persist in the merchant's inventory even after it resets.
*In general, it appears that unless you are under level 10 when you meet him, Mirmulnir will spawn at one level *higher* than the normal highest type of dragon for the player's level.  In other words, though no dragons will spawn before him, once you've met him, it will be several levels before you actually get to meet another dragon as strong as him.
** At levels 1-9, he is basically identical to a standard "Dragon".
** At levels 10-17, he has the stats of a "Blood Dragon", although Blood Dragons normally cannot start appearing until player level 18.
** At levels 18-26, he has the stats of a "Frost Dragon", which normally can't appear till player level 27. (This even changes his breath and spell type from fire to frost.)
** At levels 27-35, he has the stats of an "Elder Dragon", which normally can't appear till player level 36.
** At level 36+, he has the stats of an "Ancient Dragon", which normally can't appear until player level 45.
* Version 4.3.3 of the [[Skyrim Mod:Unofficial Skyrim Special Edition Patch|Unofficial Skyrim Special Edition Patch]] replaces the "Dohvakiin! No!!" recording with the French version.

